From de7e2473b5fedb6d687f14473ce57ecf9f5f7e26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:38:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(goals): an active goal resumes after a gateway restart

The post-turn judge queues the next goal turn in an in-memory FIFO (a local chat: an admission written after the judge ran). A restart between a turn's end and that next turn dropped it, and the goal sat active and idle until the user wrote again; only a turn running at SIGTERM was handed to the next gateway. A goal-resume watcher, started like the /loop wakeup watcher (5 s after startup, then every 15 s, each served profile's store under its scope), now queues one continuation for every active goal whose session has been idle 30 s with no running turn, queued input or pending admission. It skips paused, done, wait-parked and budget-spent goals and honors `hermes pause`, and queues once per stalled state per process. No new key.
